  {
    "slug": "resignation",
    "actor": {
      "name": "The End of Wanting — Resignation",
      "type": "npc",
      "img": "modules/kiragon-homebrew/expansions/leifs-hope/assets/portraits/resignation.png",
      "system": {
        "details": {
          "level": {
            "value": 16
          },
          "publicNotes": "<h2>The End of Wanting — Unique Creature 16</h2><p>A weary protector surrounding Leif’s Hope, who willingly hides. It believes that ending hope prevents disappointment. No demon trait.</p><p><b>AC 38, HP 295, Fort +28, Ref +25, Will +30, Perception +28.</b> <b>Crushing Certainty [one action]</b> melee +30, reach 15 ft, hit frightened 1 / critical frightened 2; no HP damage. <b>Nothing Will Change [two actions]</b> 30-ft emanation, DC 35 Will save, recharge 1d4 rounds: CS none; S frightened 1; F frightened 1, slowed 1 for 1 round; CF frightened 2, slowed 1 for 1 round, lose 1 Erosion Will. Cap extra Erosion to 1 per PC per round. <b>Remember How It Ended [reaction]</b> when a Hope Point is earned: DC 35 Will save, fail frightened 1, crit fail frightened 2; VP not removed.</p><p><b>Fractured Certainty:</b> if party deals 60 damage in a round, boss cannot use reactions until next turn, next Hope VP check gains +2 circumstance.</p><p><b>VICTORY:</b> 6 Hope Points, with three 2-point stages: Fear of Failure, Fear of Pain, Fear of Trying Again. Skill checks generally DC 31, 2 actions per check, CS 2 / S 1 / F 0 / CF -1 current barrier. Genuine personal appeal to Hope may gain a point without roll. Reducing Resignation to 0 HP only disperses it for one round, then it reforms at full HP. It cannot be killed; surrendering control of Hope ends the fight.</p>",
          "privateNotes": "KIRAGON LEIF'S HOPE: these are emotions, NOT demons. They can never be permanently killed; resolve their special win conditions. Damage is narrative/suppression only.",
